ing with the local thugs. They were actually very funny, and I could have fun with them because I was so little. At the time Iâ€™d been going through a recurring depressive illness and felt I didnâ€™t fit in at home, so I left without any clean clothing. I wanted to end my life so I decided to go to Moss Side, where the gangsters would shoot me. Of course they didnâ€™t. Iâ€™d had a very happy childhood until my father died when I was doing my O-levels, but Iâ€™ve come to the conclusion that the really bad things gave me more than they could ever take. How can you know happiness until youâ€™ve known deep sadness?</p><p><strong>Bruce Mitchell [drums]:</strong> Vini does kick off, though, properly battles. We had to section him once, and six people had to hold him down.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/jul/23/ian-curtis-the-durutti-column-factory-records-morrissey">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;7JhjInQDt2JdPzcmkwSFL20wYqLsL_vAszpy5Vv7cfEƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx9ni:///sha-256;gBXMwV2ljysCSowBZ7LNEcN2lMd3rz5FJwRIyC3oLBEƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;eWxDPUpH8zHazTOcvrIbApDSjrjizOLwTPO_8kqfdCAƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9CZ9lkFO84CPGfyTWimnSR8cGHr9Hc1-8ZbXH1DJSwMƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkefalseƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;P9AFRG8BffyaKSP_J2irkf8yvX7LQRewX5Y3frzSesAƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmarkdtrueƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;KpREbJDRqJDwARUJ7dGS8dqGxq3_TZ5n8sXX9C4r0zwƒdpairƒdleftdstarƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitƒcsumdunitdunit‚dmark`ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;_YAk07jze78spYnEgpRd4v