ime Iâ€™d been going through a recurring depressive illness and felt I didnâ€™t fit in at home, so I left without any clean clothing. I wanted to end my life so I decided to go to Moss Side, where the gangsters would shoot me. Of course they didnâ€™t. Iâ€™d had a very happy childhood until my father died when I was doing my O-levels, but Iâ€™ve come to the conclusion that the really bad things gave me more than they could ever take. How can you know happiness until youâ€™ve known deep sadness?</p><p><strong>Bruce Mitchell [drums]:</strong> Vini does kick off, though, properly battles. We had to section him once, and six people had to hold him down.</p> <a href="https://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/jul/23/ian-curtis-the-durutti-column-factory-records-morrissey">Continue reading...</a>ƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;lm4ugxfijajlyZKNyaIj0zqxJTui7Z5aln_EleYQ4JIƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxzâ€‹â€™Ian Curtis didnâ€™t have a chanceâ€™: the Durutti Column on departed friends, Factory Records and fun with Morrisseyƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;9_8dbPcTth4Acb-TzDbmGiQfh7zg1W_Q9T7-In7wlQUƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkoSyndicationItemƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;RELHirMMJSdToG0_O2KRCgt98wnrVXI8_5Y_fbiHlY4ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkxehttps://www.theguardian.com/music/2026/jul/23/ian-curtis-the-durutti-column-factory-records-morrisseyƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;GkqjUbb60l0ypfiZ7enAl3MWk-FuNEQhV-VW08UKBj8ƒdpairƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒerightdunitƒdleftdstardunit‚dmarkx`ian-curtis-didn-t-have-a-chance-the-durutti-column-on-departed-friends-factory-records-and-fun-wƒdpairƒhconstant‚dbasefEntityx9ni:///sha-256;WmyJJFJSCqXXq36wN1HpQAzdbVBF1_qzOZ